# Copy to `.env.test` (ignored by git) to run the tests, the demo, the browser suite and the budgets.
#
# These processes never read `.env`: that file is the development server's, and a machine that has one
# used to run the whole suite against its key, its bucket and its database. They read this file, and only
# this file — the address of the database SERVER they may create and drop scratch databases on.
# (`bun --no-env-file --env-file=.env.test`: a missing file is fine; CI sets the variable itself.)
#
# The compose database of `bun run db:up:postgres`. If port 5432 is taken on this machine, start it with
# `POSTGRES_PORT=55432 bun run db:up:postgres` and use the same port here (docs/CONFIG.md, Local development).
DATABASE_URL=postgres://purlay:purlay@localhost:5432/purlay
#
# Optional: the Redis of `bun run db:up:redis`, for the tests of the cloud's shared adapters (D-201). Without
# it `bun run test:all` leaves those files out, said in a banner; CI sets it and refuses without it.
# REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6379
